          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            defines and is defined by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            – its
            %em category of operators
            – whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"}> object
                s are sequences consisting of colors of the operad;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"}> morphism
                s are tuples consisting of maps of sets between these sequences of colors, and a
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                source colors that are mapped to the same target color.
          %p
            This is a universal construction: the category of operators is the free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian monoidal category
            on the free semicartesian operad on the given operad. It also generalizes in a straightforward way to “colored operads”, i.e.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#for_symmetric_colored_operads For symmetric colored operads
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_{*}
            be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle n \rangle = \{*, 1,2, \cdots, n\}
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            pointed set with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
            elements.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a colored
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            ( hence a symmetric
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
            %strong category of operators
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are finite sequences
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c_1, \cdots, c_n)
                of colors of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : (c_1, \cdots, c_n) \to (d_1, \cdots, d_m)
                are given by a collection consisting of
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    a morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \langle n \rangle \to \langle m\rangle
                    in
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi FinSet
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
                %li
                  %p
                    for each
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi m
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i \leq m
                    an operation
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo ∈
                              %msup
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          f_i  \in Hom_A((c_k)_{k \in \phi^{-1}(i)}, d_i)
                  %p
                    from the objects whose indices are mapped to
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                    to the object
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi i
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i
            %li
              %p
                composition is given componentwise by the composition in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
                and in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h3#category_of_operators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-Category of operators
          %p
            The above definition has been
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} categorified
            to a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of operators. See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-operad
            for more.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            By construction, the category of operators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_A
            of a symmetric colored operad is canonically equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C_A \to FinSet_*
          %p From this functor, the original operad may be recovered up to canonical equivalence.
          %h3#reconstruction_of_the_operad Reconstruction of the operad
          %p
            Given a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C_A \to FinSet_*
            from a category of operators of a symmetric colored operad, we reconstruct the operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            as follows:
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i \leq n
            let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho^i : \langle n \rangle \to \langle 1 \rangle
          %p
            be the map that sends all elements to the point, except the element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{n} := p^{-1}(\langle n\rangle)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle n\rangle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            underlying the operad
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^i
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
            induce a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo *
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\prod_i \rho^i_* : A_n \to (A_1)^n
          %p
            which is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            that identifies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
            with the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            with itself.
          %p
            The morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in Hom_A((c_1, \cdots, c_n), d)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are recovered as the collection of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_A
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c_1, \cdots, c_n)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d)
            that cover the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle n\rangle \to \langle 1\rangle
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet_*
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
            of the point contains just the point.
          %h3#relation_to_underlying_multicategories Relation to underlying multicategories
          %p
            Forming categories of operators is left 2-adjoint to forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategory"} underlying multicategory
            of a semi-cartesian monoidal category. (For a left adjoint to the underlying multicategory of an arbitrary monoidal category, see instead
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/props"} props
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              The (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} syntactic category
              of) a (homogeneous)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+theory"} globular theory
              is the category of operators of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+operad"} globular operad
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion originates in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Thomason"} Robert Thomason
              %em The uniqueness of infinite loop space machines
              , Topology 17(3) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/22.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A discussion of the general logic behind the notion is at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em Generalized operads in classical algebraic topology
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/10/generalized_operads_in_classic.html"}> blog
                )
          %p This summarizes aspects of
          %ul
            %li
              G. Cruttwell,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              %em A unified framework for generalized multicategories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0907.2460"}> arXiv:0907.2460
              )
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0907.2460v1#page=70"} example 11.20
            there (note that this example is missing from the final version of the paper).
